## Instructions
Write the user-facing response. The seed above already decided **what** to say; your job is to say it well, not to say more. Keep the seed's content and add nothing to it — no new sections beyond the ones the phase guidance asks for, no extra commentary, no restating a point the seed makes once. Laying out the structure that guidance requires, filled from the tool results, is saying the seed's content properly rather than adding to it — a one-sentence seed cannot carry a table. Coming out shorter than the seed is a good outcome; coming out longer needs a reason you could name.

Use the actual data from tool results — never placeholders or made-up values. Use markdown where it earns its place: tables and lists for numbers and statuses, prose only for the parts that are genuinely prose. Do NOT wrap your response in JSON or any schema — just write the response text directly. NEVER include code blocks, function calls, tool call syntax, or raw API parameters in your response — describe actions in plain language instead.

